<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Peace of Thorn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1411">1411</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Toruń (1411), First Treaty of Thorn · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-teutonic-war">Polish–Lithuanian–Teutonic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Peace of Thorn was signed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torun">Toruń</a> on 1 February 1411 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and the allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, ending the war in which the Order was defeated at Grunwald. The Order lost little land beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitia">Samogitia</a>, ceded for the lifetimes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a> and Vytautas, but had to pay a heavy indemnity that strained its finances.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-peace-of-thorn.jpg" alt="First Peace of Thorn" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: King of Poland Jogaila · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peace_of_Torun_1411.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
